# A1/A1.2/A1_15_health_and_cooking.letz
# Source: PDF slide deck "L6 (Part 1) a1convlotsmanmeli.pdf" (A1 Conversation course, Lesson 6, Part 1)
# Source: PDF slide deck "L6 (Part 2) a1convlotsmanmeli.pdf" (A1 Conversation course, Lesson 6, Part 2)
# (m)/(f)/(n)/(pl) markers stripped; "the" dropped from English glosses to match
# this course's established style. Distractor tokens are sourced from other
# entries within this same lesson (or, where noted in the report, an earlier
# A1.2 lesson's vocabulary).
# Fills added: 18 @fill blocks drilling body-part articles (gender in the
# "eppes wéi hunn" pattern), broden conjugation (stem-vowel change),
# prepositions (ouni/géint/mat/fir), negation (kee/keng), and the separable
# verb ophalen. Material mined from Part 2's grammar tables and exercises.

@lesson A1.15 "Health & Cooking"

# --- Time & degree ---
@word gëschter = yesterday
@word dréngend = urgent
@word fir d'éischt = first, firstly
@word op d'mannst = at least
@word ze vill = too much
@word ouni = without
@word géint = against

# --- Cooking verbs ---
@word beäntweren = to answer
@word broden = to fry
@word schielen = to peel
@word rappen = to grate
@word plattdrécken = to flatten
@word ofschmaachen = to season
@word zerstoussen = to crush
@word mëschen = to mix
@word muelen = to grind
@word preparéieren = to prepare
@word schëdden = to pour

# --- Cooking nouns ---
@word d'Salz = salt
@word de Peffer = pepper
@word d'Muskatnoss = nutmeg
@word d'Kraut = herb
@word d'Kraider = herbs
@word de Péiterséileg = parsley
@word d'Bratzel = chives
