# --- @fill: body-part articles in the "eppes wéi hunn" pattern ----------------
# The lesson's signature structure. The article encodes the noun's gender — the
# distractors are competing articles for the SAME body part, so the learner must
# recall masculine (de/den) vs. neuter (d') vs. feminine (d').

@fill
@lu Hatt huet [de] Kapp wéi.
@en She has a [headache].
@distractor-lu d'
@distractor-lu den
@distractor-lu eng
@distractor-en sore throat
@distractor-en stomach ache
@distractor-en backache

@fill
@lu Hie huet [de] Bauch wéi.
@en He has a [stomach ache].
@distractor-lu d'
@distractor-lu den
@distractor-lu eng
@distractor-en headache
@distractor-en sore throat
@distractor-en backache

@fill
@lu Hie huet [den] Hals wéi.
@en He has a [sore throat].
@distractor-lu de
@distractor-lu d'
@distractor-lu eng
@distractor-en headache
@distractor-en stomach ache
@distractor-en backache

@fill
@lu Si huet [de] Réck wéi.
@en She has a [backache].
@distractor-lu d'
@distractor-lu den
@distractor-lu eng
@distractor-en headache
@distractor-en toothache
@distractor-en sore throat

@fill
@lu Hatt huet [d'] Ouere wéi.
@en Her [ears] hurt.
@distractor-lu de
@distractor-lu den
@distractor-lu eng
@distractor-en throat
@distractor-en back
@distractor-en stomach

@fill
@lu Hie huet [de] Knéi wéi.
@en His [knee] hurts.
@distractor-lu d'
@distractor-lu den
@distractor-lu eng
@distractor-en foot
@distractor-en arm
@distractor-en ear

# --- @fill: broden conjugation (stem-vowel change) ----------------------------
# The irregular verb "broden" changes its stem vowel in du/hien/dir forms.
# Distractors are wrong persons of the same verb.

@fill
@lu Du [bréits] de Bifdeck an der Pan.
@en You [fry] the steak in the pan.
@distractor-lu broden
@distractor-lu bréit
@distractor-lu brot
@distractor-en fries
@distractor-en fried
@distractor-en frying

@fill
@lu Hie [bréit] d'Gromperekichelcher am Ueleg.
@en He [fries] the potato fritters in oil.
@distractor-lu broden
@distractor-lu bréits
@distractor-lu brot
@distractor-en fry
@distractor-en fried
@distractor-en frying

@fill
@lu Dir [brot] d'Kichelcher op béide Säiten.
@en You [fry] the fritters on both sides.
@distractor-lu broden
@distractor-lu bréit
@distractor-lu bréits
@distractor-en fries
@distractor-en fried
@distractor-en frying

# --- @fill: prepositions (ouni / géint / mat / fir) ---------------------------
# High-frequency prepositions from the lesson: "ouni" (without), "géint"
# (against), "mat" (with), "fir" (for). Distractors are the other prepositions
# from this same set.

@fill
@lu Da kacht [ouni] Salz!
@en Then cook [without] salt!
@distractor-lu géint
@distractor-lu mat
@distractor-lu fir
@distractor-en against
@distractor-en with
@distractor-en for

@fill
@lu Huelt eppes [géint] d'Féiwer.
@en Take something [against] the fever.
@distractor-lu ouni
@distractor-lu mat
@distractor-lu fir
@distractor-en without
@distractor-en with
@distractor-en for

@fill
@lu [Mat] Salz a Peffer ofschmaachen.
@en Season [with] salt and pepper.
@distractor-lu ouni
@distractor-lu géint
@distractor-lu fir
@distractor-en without
@distractor-en against
@distractor-en for

@fill
@lu Ech brauch e Rezept [fir] d'Medikamenter.
@en I need a prescription [for] the medications.
@distractor-lu ouni
@distractor-lu géint
@distractor-lu mat
@distractor-en without
@distractor-en against
@distractor-en with

# --- @fill: negation (kee / keng) ---------------------------------------------
# "kee" for masculine/neuter nouns, "keng" for feminine/plural. The doctor's
# advice pattern "Dann iesst kee X méi!" vs "Da lauschtert keng Y!" drills
# gender-dependent negation.

@fill
@lu Hie soll [kee] Schockela méi iessen!
@en He should stop eating [chocolate]!
@distractor-lu keng
@distractor-lu keen
@distractor-lu net
@distractor-en music
@distractor-en football
@distractor-en onions

@fill
@lu Si soll [keng] haart Musek méi lauschteren!
@en She should stop listening to loud [music]!
@distractor-lu kee
@distractor-lu keen
@distractor-lu net
@distractor-en chocolate
@distractor-en football
@distractor-en onions

@fill
@lu Hie soll [kee] Fussball méi spillen!
@en He should stop playing [football]!
@distractor-lu keng
@distractor-lu keen
@distractor-lu net
@distractor-en chocolate
@distractor-en music
@distractor-en onions

# --- @fill: separable verb "ophalen" (halt op = to stop) ----------------------
# The prefix "op" goes to the end in main clauses. Distractors are other
# separable prefixes from the lesson's vocabulary.

@fill
@lu Da [halt] op mat Fëmmen!
@en Then [stop] smoking right now!
@distractor-lu hält
@distractor-lu halen
@distractor-lu ophalen
@distractor-en stops
@distractor-en stopped
@distractor-en stopping
